    {
      "title": "Microsoft outage hits hospitals, GPs, schools and police across UK",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/13/microsoft-outage-hits-nhs-hospitals-gps-schools-and-police-across-uk",
      "description": "<p>NHS suffering ‘serious’ and widespread disruption, while people are told of possible delays in receiving prescriptions</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/live/2026/nov/13/microsoft-outage-down-today-live-update-outlook-teams-365-when-fixed-latest-status-cause-news\">Microsoft outage – live updates</a></p></li></ul><p>Vital UK services have been hit by a global Microsoft outage that left hospital staff resorting to paper records and fuelled concerns about an over-reliance on a small number of tech companies.</p><p>A day of widespread disruption sent some sectors back to the 1990s, with court staff looking for fax machines and rail travellers being warned they might not be able to rely on digital tickets.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/13/microsoft-outage-hits-nhs-hospitals-gps-schools-and-police-across-uk\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-13T18:10:05"
    },
    {
      "title": "Microsoft outage shakes up companies, schools and local governments across US",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/13/microsoft-outage-shakes-up-companies-local-governments",
      "description": "<p>Local officials warn some services remain unavailable even as Outlook starts to resume normal operations after outage</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/live/2026/nov/13/microsoft-outage-down-today-live-update-outlook-teams-365-when-fixed-latest-status-cause-news\">Microsoft outage – live updates</a></p></li></ul><p>The Microsoft Outlook outage has shaken up companies and local governments across the US that use its suite of email, calendar, video conferencing and cloud storage systems.</p><p>Even as Outlook started to resume normal operations Friday morning, local leaders from across the country, including in Miami, Maryland and Los Angeles, warned residents that certain staff or services were still unavailable due to the outage that started around 1pm ET on Thursday.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/13/microsoft-outage-shakes-up-companies-local-governments\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-13T17:17:00"
    },
